{{template "top" .}}
<div class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto custom-scroll p-6 md:p-12 flex justify-center items-start">
    <div class="w-full max-w-2xl bg-surface-container-low border border-surface-container-high rounded-sm shadow-2xl p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-on-surface">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pb-3 border-b border-surface-container-high">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[24px] text-primary">sailing</span>
            <h1 class="font-headline-md text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-on-surface">About seaRoute</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
            seaRoute is a tactical maritime ECDIS route and waypoint calculator built for maritime navigators, voyage planners, and developers. It calculates shortest feasible sea passages across global maritime shipping routes using Dijkstra and A* heuristics over high-resolution ocean graph networks.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4 rounded-sm border border-surface-container-high flex flex-col gap-2">
            <span class="text-primary font-bold text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider">Engine Specifications</span>
            <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-surface-container/50 py-1 text-on-surface-variant">
                <span>Core Algorithm</span>
                <span class="text-on-surface font-semibold">Dijkstra &amp; A* (Heuristic Graph Engine)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-surface-container/50 py-1 text-on-surface-variant">
                <span>Passage Constraints</span>
                <span class="text-on-surface font-semibold">Suez, Panama, Malacca, Kiel, Dover &amp; 9 Chokepoints</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-surface-container/50 py-1 text-on-surface-variant">
                <span>Marine Regulations</span>
                <span class="text-tertiary font-semibold">IMO MARPOL Annex VI Reg 14 ECA / SECA</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between py-1 text-on-surface-variant">
                <span>Developer</span>
                <span class="text-primary font-semibold">CaptV89</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4 rounded-sm border border-warning/40 flex flex-col gap-2">
            <span class="text-warning font-bold text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider">Limitations</span>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 list-disc pl-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
                <li>TSS data is community-maintained (OpenSeaMap / OpenStreetMap) and its coverage is incomplete. Stretches near land outside the covered areas are flagged <span class="text-on-surface">tss-unknown</span>; where TSS rules leave no route, the flagged <span class="text-on-surface">tss-unresolved</span> stretch ignores one scheme.</li>
                <li>The land data is simplified (50 m) and covers a corridor around the MARNET network. Canals and channels narrower than that read as aground and are flagged as hazards. MARNET itself is not a surveyed track.</li>
                <li>A licensed ENC (S-57/S-101 from a hydrographic office or chart distributor) is the authoritative source for charted hazards and traffic schemes. seaRoute does not use one.</li>
                <li>Depths come from GEBCO 2026 and land from OpenStreetMap. Both are approximate and not for navigation; check the official chart.</li>
                <li>Vessel inputs are draught (default 10 m), speed (default 14 kn) and vessel type (tanker, bulk, general or container; default bulk). The route needs water at least as deep as draught + squat + margin. Squat follows Barrass, Cb &times; V&sup2; / 100 metres in open water and Cb &times; V&sup2; / 50 in a canal or strait (Cb: tanker 0.80, bulk 0.80, general 0.70, container 0.60; V in knots). The margin for depth data error is the larger of 2 m and 10% of the draught. Passages with a draught limit close when the vessel needs more. Near each port, the first stretch up to 15 NM is exempt until the track first reaches safe water.</li>
                <li>The Kiel Canal limit (9.5 m) applies to ships up to about 160 m length. Longer ships face lower limits, which are not modelled here.</li>
                <li>seaRoute is not for navigation. A passage plan still needs official charts.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Land and Traffic Separation Scheme data: &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL
            (<a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openstreetmap.org/copyright</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Depth data: GEBCO Bathymetric Compilation Group (2026) GEBCO 2026 Grid
            (<a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="https://doi.org/10.5285/4f68d5c7-45eb-f999-e063-7086abc036fa" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.5285/4f68d5c7-45eb-f999-e063-7086abc036fa</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Forecast data: ECMWF IFS open data, CC BY 4.0
            (<a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0</a>).
            Forecasts are not for navigation.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2 flex items-center justify-between">
            <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-1 text-primary hover:underline">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">arrow_back</span> Return to Chart
            </a>
            <a href="https://github.com/captv89/seaRoute" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="flex items-center gap-1 text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-surface">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">code</span> GitHub Repository
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{{template "bottom" .}}

